            <ArticleTitle>Rupture of rudimentary horn pregnancy at the 15th week of gestation: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>209-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with acute abdomen at 15th week of gestation underwent an emergency laparatomy. A ruptured rudimentary horn pregnancy was diagnosed, and the rudimentary part including the fetus and the accessories was resected. The mother survived without any complications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
